
# PRF PREPROCESSING PIPELINE
# University of Louisville  |  Renal Failure Project 2026
# PRF definition

# Approved preprocessing steps (Steps 1–17, plus new steps noted above):
#   1.  Exclude patients on preoperative dialysis
#   2.  Exclude patients with baseline creatinine >= 4 mg/dL
#   3.  Drop columns with > 50% missing data
#   4.  Delete rows missing low-missingness variables (numeric ≤1%, categorical ≤2%)
#   5.  Deduplicate: keep most recent surgery per patient
#   6.  Drop near-zero-variance categorical columns (< 1% positive cases)
#   7.  Combine chronic lung disease severity + type into one variable
#   8.  Remove hematocrit, height, weight (collinear with Hgb and BMI)
#   9.  Drop Last A1C Level (~9% missing; correlated with diabetes and age)
#   9b. Drop MELD Score (derived score; per collaborator instruction) [NEW]
#   10. Log-transform Platelet Count (highly right-skewed)
#   CABG/VALVE. Include iff CAB (planned/unplanned) OR Valve == "Yes" [NEW]
#   11. [BP] Align BP readings to most recent surgery per patient
#   12. [BP] Remove postoperative rows with missing SBP
#   13. Stratified 70/30 train-test split (createDataPartition) — run per case
#   14. [Train only] Random Under-Sampling (RUS) — 10:1 neg:pos ratio
#   15. [Train only] Z-score normalisation (fit on train, applied to test)
#   16. [Train only] SMOTE-NC (k=5) — double the minority class
#   17. k-1 dummy encoding of all categorical variables

# 0. SETUP 
